00:56:23,033 --> 00:56:24,300
Well, goodbye now.

1509
00:56:24,333 --> 00:56:25,567
- Bye.
- [Dad groans]

1510
00:56:25,600 --> 00:56:27,333
[Crow mimics groan]

1511
00:56:27,367 --> 00:56:28,733
You think
he'd ever accuse US?

1512
00:56:28,767 --> 00:56:31,333
--Changed these last few weeks.
Have you noticed it, Dan?

1513
00:56:31,367 --> 00:56:34,267
- Jimmy who?
- Yeah, he seems to have
grown up overnight.

1514
00:56:34,300 --> 00:56:35,967
Well, I don't like it.

1515
00:56:36,000 --> 00:56:38,433
What do you suppose he's doing
out every night in the week?

1516
00:56:38,467 --> 00:56:40,367
For several nights,
he didn't come home at all.

1517
00:56:40,400 --> 00:56:43,533
Maybe he stayed
with a friend.

1518
00:56:43,567 --> 00:56:46,167
It's a little late to start
asking questions now.

1519
00:56:46,200 --> 00:56:47,800
Well, after all,
your his father.

1520
00:56:47,833 --> 00:56:48,900
You ought to
keep an eye on him.

1521
00:56:48,933 --> 00:56:50,433
Well, you're his mother.

1522
00:56:50,467 --> 00:56:52,767
You stay home once in a while,
you might know what he's up to.

1523
00:56:52,800 --> 00:56:54,567
The talking corpse,
ladies and gentlemen.

1524
00:56:54,600 --> 00:56:56,567
--A girlfriend, that's all.

1525
00:56:56,600 --> 00:56:57,867
I had when I was his age.

1526
00:56:57,900 --> 00:56:59,433
And then I died inside.

1527
00:56:59,467 --> 00:57:01,267
--Taking after you.

1528
00:57:01,300 --> 00:57:03,200
That's it,
there's a six-pack

1529
00:57:03,233 --> 00:57:04,933
calling my name.

1530
00:57:10,667 --> 00:57:12,000
- Hello, kitty.
- Quack, quack, quack.

1531
00:57:12,033 --> 00:57:13,800
I brought you
a little something.

1532
00:57:13,833 --> 00:57:15,367
- Quack quack quack.
- Oh, Jimmy.

1533
00:57:15,400 --> 00:57:16,933
- Leftover Chinese!
- Not another present!

1534
00:57:16,967 --> 00:57:18,633
Why, sure. I like buying
presents for you.

1535
00:57:18,667 --> 00:57:20,667
- It's fun.
- But I always have
to pay for them.

1536
00:57:20,700 --> 00:57:22,833
Jimmy, I don't want you
to be offended,

1537
00:57:22,867 --> 00:57:24,100
but I've got
to ask you something.

1538
00:57:24,133 --> 00:57:25,733
Do I have a weird profile?

1539
00:57:25,767 --> 00:57:27,867
--Mixed up in anything that
isn't quite on the level,
are you?

1540
00:57:27,900 --> 00:57:29,100
Whatever gave you that idea?

1541
00:57:29,133 --> 00:57:30,800
I'm just selling drugs
to school kids.

1542
00:57:30,833 --> 00:57:33,167
--Except that you have so much
more money to spend lately.

1543
00:57:33,200 --> 00:57:34,600
- Oh, the mob ties.
- Look,

1544
00:57:34,633 --> 00:57:35,833
don't you worry about me.

1545
00:57:35,867 --> 00:57:37,200
I wouldn't do
anything that wasn't

1546
00:57:37,233 --> 00:57:38,733
on the right side
of the law.

1547
00:57:38,767 --> 00:57:40,267
I hope not, Jimmy.

1548
00:57:40,300 --> 00:57:42,333
You're so sweet, I wouldn't
want you to change.

1549
00:57:42,367 --> 00:57:44,467
- Why should I change?
- I'll always wear
jed clampett's hat.

1550
00:57:44,500 --> 00:57:45,900
People do in this town.

1551
00:57:45,933 --> 00:57:48,700
- Circle pines'll do that.
- --You don't, kitty.

1552
00:57:48,733 --> 00:57:52,400
Now let me have
that tongue of yours.

1553
00:57:52,433 --> 00:57:53,667
Say, Eddie Mendez gave me

1554
00:57:53,700 --> 00:57:54,900
two tickets for
the follies Sunday.

1555
00:57:54,933 --> 00:57:57,333
Hey, what do I bid for two
tickets to follies? Hey!

1556
00:57:57,367 --> 00:57:58,700
--Cancel that like you did
our luncheon date today?

1557
00:57:58,733 --> 00:58:01,100
Oh, now, look, kitten.
Can I help it if I'm busy?

1558
00:58:01,133 --> 00:58:02,467
I'm hanged
if I can find time

1559
00:58:02,500 --> 00:58:03,900
to do the things
we've planned.

1560
00:58:03,933 --> 00:58:05,433
But business
is sure picking up.

1561
00:58:05,467 --> 00:58:07,800
- Well, that's good.
- You bet, for both of US.

1562
00:58:07,833 --> 00:58:09,000
The higher
Charlie Blake goes...

1563
00:58:09,033 --> 00:58:10,767
- The higher kitty Reed.
- You said it.

1564
00:58:10,800 --> 00:58:12,733
Well, bye, darling.

1565
00:58:12,767 --> 00:58:14,833
Oh, uh, I meant
to ask you before.

1566
00:58:14,867 --> 00:58:16,533
Have you put
Jimmy Wilson to work?

1567
00:58:16,567 --> 00:58:19,067
Why, uh, I haven't laid eyes
on him-- have you seen him?

1568
00:58:19,100 --> 00:58:21,367
[All] * liar! Liar!

1569
00:58:21,400 --> 00:58:22,900
--You asked me to give you
a buildup, remember?

1570
00:58:22,933 --> 00:58:24,100
Must've been a swell buildup

1571
00:58:24,133 --> 00:58:25,433
you gave him to
keep him away like this.

1572
00:58:25,467 --> 00:58:27,733
Man, everybody lies
in this movie.

1573
00:58:27,767 --> 00:58:29,533
--By now, he'd be pounding
on your door for a job.

1574
00:58:29,567 --> 00:58:30,767
Well, I haven't seen him.

1575
00:58:30,800 --> 00:58:32,133
I guess he's pounding
on the wrong door.

1576
00:58:32,167 --> 00:58:33,600
- You said it.
- Hey, you talk about

1577
00:58:33,633 --> 00:58:35,500
me giving you a stand-up--

1578
00:58:35,533 --> 00:58:37,767
where have you been disappearing
to after the show every night?

1579
00:58:37,800 --> 00:58:40,233
You sure get out of that
dressing room in a hurry.

1580
00:58:40,267 --> 00:58:41,500
And I've been missing you.

1581
00:58:41,533 --> 00:58:43,267
Well, Charlie,
you know the old saying.

1582
00:58:43,300 --> 00:58:45,667
Early to bed
and early to rise.

1583
00:58:45,700 --> 00:58:47,967
- Huh?
- That's me. Bye, now.
- Goodbye.

1584
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:49,633
I also know about
a bird in the hand.

1585
00:58:49,667 --> 00:58:52,300
Now, get out of here.
"Early to bed and early..."

1586
00:58:52,333 --> 00:58:53,933
You're new with Mr. Blake.

1587
00:58:53,967 --> 00:58:55,467
How long have you
been with him?

1588
00:58:55,500 --> 00:58:57,433
A few weeks-- I'm not working
full-time for him yet.

1589
00:58:57,467 --> 00:58:59,000
Mmm, I see.

1590
00:58:59,033 --> 00:59:00,667
I'll be with you
in a minute.

1591
00:59:00,700 --> 00:59:03,167
Uh, note to self.
Find out correct time.

1592
00:59:05,633 --> 00:59:07,633
Uh, it's my birthday
tomorrow, mister.

1593
00:59:10,267 --> 00:59:12,400
What is this guy,
butcher to the mob?

1594
00:59:14,233 --> 00:59:15,867
Here you go.
Happy birthday, Jimmy.

1595
00:59:15,900 --> 00:59:17,467
This is very important.

1596
00:59:17,500 --> 00:59:20,367
You see that Mr. Blake
gets this note tonight.

1597
00:59:20,400 --> 00:59:22,767
And be sure that you
give it to no one but him.

1598
00:59:22,800 --> 00:59:24,000
All right, I'll do that.

1599
00:59:24,033 --> 00:59:27,500
And this is skag.
Be careful with it.

1600
00:59:27,533 --> 00:59:29,300
I'll let you out
the back door.

1601
00:59:29,333 --> 00:59:32,167
Don't tell the Nazis
where I am.

1602
00:59:38,833 --> 00:59:40,000
Hi, I have
an important thing

1603
00:59:40,033 --> 00:59:42,633
and some stuff called skag?

1604
00:59:42,667 --> 00:59:43,900
What's the idea
coming back here?

1605
00:59:43,933 --> 00:59:45,267
I told you what to do
with that package.

1606
00:59:45,300 --> 00:59:47,167
I know you did, Mr. Blake,
but Mr. Carlton said

1607
00:59:47,200 --> 00:59:48,633
to give you this note.
He said it was important.

1608
00:59:48,667 --> 00:59:51,100
Is this a caper?

1609
00:59:51,133 --> 00:59:54,833
Never should've gone
to old country buffet with him.

1610
00:59:54,867 --> 00:59:56,233
Let's see,
what does it say here?

1611
00:59:56,267 --> 00:59:59,200
"Isn't this guy carrying
the letter a dink?"

1612
01:00:00,867 --> 01:00:02,700
It's all right, Jimmy,
you did the right thing.

1613
01:00:02,733 --> 01:00:03,867
Better wait out
in the other office.

1614
01:00:03,900 --> 01:00:05,267
I may have something else
for you to do.

1615
01:00:05,300 --> 01:00:06,533
Okay, Mr. Blake.

1616
01:00:06,567 --> 01:00:08,633
And, uh, do some filing
while you're out there.

1617
01:00:11,967 --> 01:00:14,333
Huh, yeah,
I got a real knack

1618
01:00:14,367 --> 01:00:16,900
for shadowy errands.
That's me.

1619
01:00:20,033 --> 01:00:21,233
All right, boys, come on in.

1620
01:00:21,267 --> 01:00:22,767
We're gonna
pants the courier.

1621
01:00:22,800 --> 01:00:24,533
William Frawley!
Montgomery clift!

1622
01:00:24,567 --> 01:00:26,300
Get this. "Chuck,

1623
01:00:26,333 --> 01:00:27,567
"I tried to get the painting

1624
01:00:27,600 --> 01:00:29,200
"out of Gordon's
dead storage.

1625
01:00:29,233 --> 01:00:31,367
"Couldn't make it as
the place is being watched.

1626
01:00:31,400 --> 01:00:33,200
"Don't send
any more packages.

1627
01:00:33,233 --> 01:00:35,600
"I'm leaving town.
Take my tip and do the same.

1628
01:00:35,633 --> 01:00:37,200
- Carl."
- well, how do you
like that?

1629
01:00:37,233 --> 01:00:39,267
- He called you Chuck.
- I thought that stuff
was safe there.

1630
01:00:39,300 --> 01:00:41,033
$30,000 worth of diamonds.

1631
01:00:41,067 --> 01:00:42,300
What're you gonna
do now, Charlie?

1632
01:00:42,333 --> 01:00:43,633
We're gonna talk
like dis, see?

1633
01:00:43,667 --> 01:00:44,867
-- To the warehouse
and get it out.

1634
01:00:44,900 --> 01:00:46,300
Tonight, and take
the kid with you.

1635
01:00:46,333 --> 01:00:47,800
Take the kid? What for?

1636
01:00:47,833 --> 01:00:49,267
May take two of you
to do the job.

1637
01:00:49,300 --> 01:00:50,867
I'll have him run a car,
and he can drive for you.

1638
01:00:50,900 --> 01:00:54,300
I'm due on
the Superman set now.

1639
01:00:54,333 --> 01:00:55,667
- Oh, Jimmy.
- Oh hi!

1640
01:00:55,700 --> 01:00:57,367
I want you to go down
to Olson's before it closes

1641
01:00:57,400 --> 01:00:58,733
and rent a car.

1642
01:00:58,767 --> 01:01:00,133
Come back here
at 12:00 tonight

1643
01:01:00,167 --> 01:01:01,400
and pick up the boys,
and take them down

1644
01:01:01,433 --> 01:01:03,567
to Gordon's warehouse
to pick up a package.

1645
01:01:03,600 --> 01:01:05,233
Then drive them back here.

1646
01:01:05,267 --> 01:01:06,667
Okay, Mr. Blake.

1647
01:01:06,700 --> 01:01:09,400
He's got framed
rubber vomit on the wall.

1648
01:01:11,033 --> 01:01:12,900
You know what,
I should call Mr. Blake

1649
01:01:12,933 --> 01:01:14,867
and tell him
how much I like him.

1650
01:01:17,933 --> 01:01:19,467
Hello, kitty?
This is Jimmy,

1651
01:01:19,500 --> 01:01:21,033
remember me?
I'm your boyfriend.

1652
01:01:21,067 --> 01:01:22,367
You'd better be.

1653
01:01:22,400 --> 01:01:23,800
Can I see you tonight?
We'll go dancing.

1654
01:01:23,833 --> 01:01:25,633
Oh, this is late-night hot.

1655
01:01:25,667 --> 01:01:26,900
Oh, swell.

1656
01:01:26,933 --> 01:01:28,500
I've got a little business
to take care of,

1657
01:01:28,533 --> 01:01:30,267
and I'll be about
half an hour late.

1658
01:01:30,300 --> 01:01:32,000
I've got something
awfully important to ask you.

1659
01:01:32,033 --> 01:01:34,433
Now, don't tell me
you're going to propose to me.

1660
01:01:34,467 --> 01:01:36,467
- Maybe.
- All right, hon,
I'll be looking for you.

1661
01:01:36,500 --> 01:01:38,967
Jimmy's cheating on me!

1662
01:01:39,000 --> 01:01:42,167
That guy's eaves-dropping
on his eaves-dropping.

1663
01:01:42,200 --> 01:01:43,533
Wait here, I'll be back
in an hour.

1664
01:01:43,567 --> 01:01:45,367
With squeaky shoes on.

1665
01:01:49,733 --> 01:01:51,900
[Joel]
* love came between US

1666
01:01:54,233 --> 01:01:55,567
quack, quack.
Quack-quack quack.

1667
01:01:55,600 --> 01:01:58,033
Oh, hello. I didn't expect
to see you, Charlie.

1668
01:01:58,067 --> 01:02:00,133
I know you didn't.
You expected the kid.

1669
01:02:00,167 --> 01:02:02,767
Nobody expects
to see Charlie!

1670
01:02:02,800 --> 01:02:05,067
* love came between US

1671
01:02:05,100 --> 01:02:06,633
oh, uh, buttermints, huh?

1672
01:02:06,667 --> 01:02:09,433
Don't mind if I do. Mmm.

1673
01:02:09,467 --> 01:02:12,367
First of all, you and I are
gonna straighten out something.

1674
01:02:12,400 --> 01:02:14,133
What's going on
between you two?

1675
01:02:14,167 --> 01:02:15,933
Uh, cheap love. Why?

1676
01:02:15,967 --> 01:02:17,833
I don't know what you're
talking about, Charlie.

1677
01:02:17,867 --> 01:02:19,967
Why is she dressed like
major Barbara?

1678
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:21,533
No?

1679
01:02:21,567 --> 01:02:23,500
- Well, I'll make it clear.
- [Joel mumbles]

1680
01:02:23,533 --> 01:02:26,667
I heard that phone conversation
you had a little while ago.

1681
01:02:26,700 --> 01:02:28,233
He was talking
from my office.

1682
01:02:28,267 --> 01:02:30,033
It was funny.
Made me laugh-- hah!

1683
01:02:30,067 --> 01:02:32,300
So you really
fell in love with the kid.

1684
01:02:32,333 --> 01:02:34,167
Now, look.

1685
01:02:34,200 --> 01:02:36,467
Nobody's gonna
take you away from me.

1686
01:02:36,500 --> 01:02:38,467
- Nobody.
- Not even me, see?

1687
01:02:38,500 --> 01:02:39,867
I'll kill me
before that happens.

1688
01:02:39,900 --> 01:02:42,233
Why... why, Charlie.

1689
01:02:42,267 --> 01:02:45,133
You don't really think
I fell for that kid, do you?

1690
01:02:45,167 --> 01:02:47,067
Why, you asked me
to string him along.

1691
01:02:47,100 --> 01:02:48,633
Can I help it
if he fell for me?

1692
01:02:48,667 --> 01:02:51,967
Well, he did win
that essay contest.

1693
01:02:52,000 --> 01:02:53,433
He's as good as forgotten.

1694
01:02:53,467 --> 01:02:56,267
[All] * liar! Liar!

1695
01:02:56,300 --> 01:02:58,800
When he gets here,
I want you to get rid of him.

1696
01:02:58,833 --> 01:03:01,067
- Your way.
- Or the highway.

1697
01:03:01,100 --> 01:03:03,433
Or would you rather
have me do it?

1698
01:03:03,467 --> 01:03:04,667
Okay, Charlie.

1699
01:03:04,700 --> 01:03:06,167
I'll be happy in my work.

1700
01:03:06,200 --> 01:03:07,900
It ought to be a cinch.

1701
01:03:07,933 --> 01:03:11,100
- [Door buzzes]
- Oh, it's the three
hard-boiled eggs she ordered.

1702
01:03:11,133 --> 01:03:12,367
I'll be in there listening.

1703
01:03:12,400 --> 01:03:15,333
Like I usually am.

1704
01:03:15,367 --> 01:03:16,967
Watch out! Aah!

1705
01:03:17,000 --> 01:03:19,367
- [All mimic crash]
- [Doorbell buzzes]

1706
01:03:21,267 --> 01:03:24,100
[Servo muffled]
Hey, I thought you were gonna
have this stuff dry-cleaned.

1707
01:03:24,133 --> 01:03:26,233
Well, aren't I miss popular?

1708
01:03:28,600 --> 01:03:30,367
Well, I've joined
the black hand. Hi!

1709
01:03:30,400 --> 01:03:31,900
--Let's get going.
We've only got a few hours.

1710
01:03:31,933 --> 01:03:34,467
I have some work to do
later on.

1711
01:03:34,500 --> 01:03:36,200
I'm not going.

1712
01:03:36,233 --> 01:03:39,367
Well, what the--
wait a minute!

1713
01:03:39,400 --> 01:03:41,267
Hey, are you kidding?
Why, over the phone,

1714
01:03:41,300 --> 01:03:42,833
you just got through
saying we'd go someplace.

1715
01:03:42,867 --> 01:03:45,367
[Joel as Schwarzenegger]
I lied.

1716
01:03:45,400 --> 01:03:46,767
I know,
but after I talked to you,

1717
01:03:46,800 --> 01:03:48,600
- I changed my mind.
- Guy in the closet.

1718
01:03:48,633 --> 01:03:50,000
An old friend of mine called,

1719
01:03:50,033 --> 01:03:51,833
- and I'm going out with him.
- Guy in the closet.

1720
01:03:51,867 --> 01:03:53,133
Hey, you say that so
convincingly,

1721
01:03:53,167 --> 01:03:54,700
I almost believe it.

1722
01:03:54,733 --> 01:03:56,067
[Crow muffled]
Hey, where'd you get
these golf clubs?

1723
01:03:56,100 --> 01:03:57,267
- Shh!
- You can believe it.

1724
01:03:57,300 --> 01:03:58,633
Guy in the closet.

1725
01:03:58,667 --> 01:03:59,967
- Do you mean it?
- Closet.

1726
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:02,033
Of course I mean it.

1727
01:04:02,067 --> 01:04:03,500
Hey, I smell Italian.

1728
01:04:03,533 --> 01:04:05,100
- Look, wh--
- oh, you poor chump.

1729
01:04:05,133 --> 01:04:06,467
[Crow as Bert lahr]
Courage!

1730
01:04:06,500 --> 01:04:09,267
Did you really
take me seriously?

1731
01:04:09,300 --> 01:04:11,200
Did you think for one minute
that I loved you?

1732
01:04:11,233 --> 01:04:12,900
That I wanted to marry you?

1733
01:04:12,933 --> 01:04:14,200
She's smokin'.

1734
01:04:14,233 --> 01:04:15,700
Why could you imagine
kitty Reed

1735
01:04:15,733 --> 01:04:17,433
cooped up in a little
two-by-four cottage

1736
01:04:17,467 --> 01:04:19,267
with a string of kids
climbing all over her?

1737
01:04:19,300 --> 01:04:20,667
Oh, no, not kitty.

1738
01:04:20,700 --> 01:04:21,867
I am the angel of death.

1739
01:04:21,900 --> 01:04:23,000
The day of reckoning
is upon US.

1740
01:04:23,033 --> 01:04:24,300
--Jimmy, I thought
that for a while

1741
01:04:24,333 --> 01:04:26,400
you might go someplace.

1742
01:04:26,433 --> 01:04:28,167
But you'll always
be a shoe salesman

1743
01:04:28,200 --> 01:04:30,500
- at 25 a week.
