Oh, that seems reasonable.

1987
01:13:23,167 --> 01:13:24,867
Walk back with a couple
of nice fellas.

1988
01:13:24,900 --> 01:13:26,933
And then all of a sudden,
you-- whoa!

1989
01:13:29,067 --> 01:13:30,433
This is a message
from the other kids

1990
01:13:30,467 --> 01:13:32,700
in the essay contest, Jimmy.

1991
01:13:32,733 --> 01:13:35,233
So I told her that
I like playtex-- wha?

1992
01:13:35,267 --> 01:13:37,667
Huh?

1993
01:13:37,700 --> 01:13:40,133
Jimmy's really fitting in with
the other gangsters his age.

1994
01:13:40,167 --> 01:13:41,367
Hey, wait a minute,
somebody's coming.

1995
01:13:41,400 --> 01:13:42,633
- Let's get out of here.
- Mobsters

1996
01:13:42,667 --> 01:13:44,967
are easily scared.

1997
01:13:45,000 --> 01:13:47,633
Wait, I forgot to give you
the stuff here.

1998
01:13:50,533 --> 01:13:52,167
What's a matter, kid?
What happened to you?

1999
01:13:52,200 --> 01:13:54,233
- I don't know.
- You'd better
come along with US.

2000
01:13:54,267 --> 01:13:55,400
We'll report it
to the police.

2001
01:13:55,433 --> 01:13:56,600
No, no, fellas, just--

2002
01:13:56,633 --> 01:13:58,100
just help me find a cab,
will you?

2003
01:13:58,133 --> 01:14:00,567
- I wanna go home.
- Okay, kid, just as you say.

2004
01:14:00,600 --> 01:14:02,467
Alfred on the spot.

2005
01:14:05,767 --> 01:14:07,233
Mom? Dad?

2006
01:14:07,267 --> 01:14:09,367
I won the "get the crap
kicked out of you" contest!

2007
01:14:09,400 --> 01:14:11,533
Mom? Dad?

2008
01:14:11,567 --> 01:14:13,333
I'm up here, honey,
with the dt's!

2009
01:14:13,367 --> 01:14:15,433
Could you get the yellow lizard
out of the bathroom?

2010
01:14:18,267 --> 01:14:19,733
Uh, where's the dexedrine?

2011
01:14:19,767 --> 01:14:22,633
Where's that dexedrine?

2012
01:14:22,667 --> 01:14:24,900
If knick-knacks
ruled the world.

2013
01:14:28,833 --> 01:14:30,300
- [Phone rings]
- Meanwhile,

2014
01:14:30,333 --> 01:14:31,767
at black panther
headquarters.

2015
01:14:31,800 --> 01:14:35,000
I'll see. What have you got?

2016
01:14:35,033 --> 01:14:36,300
[Servo] Yyyyes?

2017
01:14:36,333 --> 01:14:38,400
Hello. Yes, sir?

2018
01:14:38,433 --> 01:14:40,400
Mr. Wilson in?
Tell him his son wants him.

2019
01:14:40,433 --> 01:14:42,367
Just a minute, I'll see.

2020
01:14:42,400 --> 01:14:44,167
Ollie, telephone.

2021
01:14:44,200 --> 01:14:45,700
I've never had such luck.

2022
01:14:45,733 --> 01:14:47,833
- Murray, use a coaster.
- --You beat me every hand.

2023
01:14:47,867 --> 01:14:49,467
Your boy's on the phone,
Mr. Wilson.

2024
01:14:49,500 --> 01:14:51,400
- He wants to talk to you.
- Tell him I'm not here.

2025
01:14:51,433 --> 01:14:53,033
But you are-- oh.

2026
01:14:53,067 --> 01:14:55,767
- Come on, deal.
- Yes, sir.

2027
01:14:55,800 --> 01:14:57,100
He says he's not here.

2028
01:14:57,133 --> 01:14:59,567
I'm sorry, sir,
but your father isn't here.

2029
01:14:59,600 --> 01:15:03,267
Well, if he comes in,
tell him I called, will you?

2030
01:15:03,300 --> 01:15:05,000
Uh, I wonder who that was
in the background.

2031
01:15:05,033 --> 01:15:07,733
Oh, well. Mom!

2032
01:15:07,767 --> 01:15:09,900
[Crow sobs] I'm just
gonna run away!

2033
01:15:12,933 --> 01:15:15,000
I got peanut butter.
And underwear.

2034
01:15:15,033 --> 01:15:17,900
And that's all I need!

2035
01:15:17,933 --> 01:15:20,167
[Joel sobs] Well, I'm gonna
run away to Kansas

2036
01:15:20,200 --> 01:15:22,467
and become a ventriloquist.

2037
01:15:25,967 --> 01:15:27,500
[Crow sobs]

2038
01:15:27,533 --> 01:15:29,233
Oh, wait a minute.

2039
01:15:29,267 --> 01:15:31,933
Where's my trowel-sized
pert shampoo?

2040
01:15:31,967 --> 01:15:33,633
Jimmy is suddenly seized

2041
01:15:33,667 --> 01:15:37,200
with an essay idea.

2042
01:15:37,233 --> 01:15:40,567
Say, that's what happened
to all his other moms.

2043
01:15:46,333 --> 01:15:48,200
"Problem with mob. On lamb.

2044
01:15:48,233 --> 01:15:51,133
Accusingly yours,
Jimmy."

2045
01:15:51,167 --> 01:15:53,333
"P.s. Hope you had fun

2046
01:15:53,367 --> 01:15:55,633
at Jack Taylor's."

2047
01:15:59,100 --> 01:16:01,567
Would you comb your hair?
That's annoying.

2048
01:16:01,600 --> 01:16:04,233
I'll just put this over here
with mom's suicide note.

2049
01:16:05,567 --> 01:16:08,400
Oh, they'll think
it's a cocktail napkin.

2050
01:16:10,600 --> 01:16:13,300
I saw some kick-ass
parties here.

2051
01:16:17,333 --> 01:16:20,900
** [all sing "boots are
made for walking" intro]

2052
01:16:24,033 --> 01:16:26,200
More powerful
than a locomotive!

2053
01:16:30,333 --> 01:16:32,267
Auntie em! Auntie em!

2054
01:16:36,067 --> 01:16:38,900
- What, is he thinking
about trains now?
- Uh, yeah.

2055
01:16:38,933 --> 01:16:41,500
These trains never
stop for you.

2056
01:16:41,533 --> 01:16:42,867
Ah, but he's able to...

2057
01:16:42,900 --> 01:16:46,400
Pick up a ride
with the joad family.

2058
01:16:46,433 --> 01:16:49,000
This is the life.

2059
01:16:49,033 --> 01:16:50,867
[Joel laughs]

2060
01:16:53,333 --> 01:16:55,600
Maybe I'll travel somewhere.

2061
01:17:01,167 --> 01:17:02,667
Hey, cafe.

2062
01:17:02,700 --> 01:17:04,433
I've heard of this place.

2063
01:17:06,833 --> 01:17:08,633
I don't know if I'll find
any Thai food

2064
01:17:08,667 --> 01:17:10,233
in this old town.

2065
01:17:12,633 --> 01:17:14,733
Hey, maybe they'll see me
looking dejected

2066
01:17:14,767 --> 01:17:18,233
and invite me in.

2067
01:17:18,267 --> 01:17:20,900
On top of it all,
my area's gone.

2068
01:17:24,400 --> 01:17:25,667
Boy, that was good stuff.

2069
01:17:25,700 --> 01:17:27,367
I gotta learn to order
only one chicken.

2070
01:17:27,400 --> 01:17:29,367
Oh, and that
whipped cream? Mmm.

2071
01:17:32,933 --> 01:17:34,833
One million, two million.

2072
01:17:34,867 --> 01:17:37,733
Three million, four million.

2073
01:17:39,667 --> 01:17:43,300
14 billion, 15 billion.

2074
01:17:43,333 --> 01:17:45,833
I've decided-- I'm gonna
do something really stupid.

2075
01:17:52,033 --> 01:17:55,100
Um, uh, can I Rob you?

2076
01:17:55,133 --> 01:17:56,833
- Cup of coffee.
- You bet.

2077
01:17:56,867 --> 01:17:59,767
And put the French silk pie
in an unmarked bag.

2078
01:17:59,800 --> 01:18:01,200
Expecting somebody?

2079
01:18:01,233 --> 01:18:03,333
- No.
- I didn't know it was drugs!

2080
01:18:06,833 --> 01:18:08,700
Uh, do you have any bullets?

2081
01:18:08,733 --> 01:18:10,100
How about a hamburger?

2082
01:18:10,133 --> 01:18:11,333
It's what's for dinner.

2083
01:18:11,367 --> 01:18:12,867
No thanks, I'm not hungry.

2084
01:18:12,900 --> 01:18:14,433
If you're broke,
it's on the house.

2085
01:18:14,467 --> 01:18:16,567
Hey, it's officer tootie.

2086
01:18:16,600 --> 01:18:18,533
Plenty of onions, eh?

2087
01:18:18,567 --> 01:18:20,233
French fries,
and all the trimmings.

2088
01:18:20,267 --> 01:18:22,800
I'll trust you.
You can pay me anytime you want.

2089
01:18:22,833 --> 01:18:25,300
- Ooh ooh.
- Okay.

2090
01:18:25,333 --> 01:18:28,567
Did someone tell you
it was my birthday?

2091
01:18:28,600 --> 01:18:32,200
You like my hat? I made it.

2092
01:18:32,233 --> 01:18:34,133
Give and take,
that's my system.

2093
01:18:34,167 --> 01:18:36,033
- Yep.
- Share what you've got,

2094
01:18:36,067 --> 01:18:37,933
and you'll never want.

2095
01:18:37,967 --> 01:18:40,367
I've had a lot of guys
come in here broke.

2096
01:18:40,400 --> 01:18:41,867
Never sent 'em away hungry.

2097
01:18:41,900 --> 01:18:43,233
Got 'em piled out back.

2098
01:18:43,267 --> 01:18:45,233
And I don't lose
by it either.

2099
01:18:45,267 --> 01:18:47,333
They always
come back and pay.

2100
01:18:47,367 --> 01:18:48,800
Most people are okay.

2101
01:18:48,833 --> 01:18:51,000
Except for you, of course.

2102
01:18:51,033 --> 01:18:53,633
Here, stab this
into your thigh.

2103
01:18:53,667 --> 01:18:56,633
You're not gonna
hug me, are you?

2104
01:18:56,667 --> 01:18:58,100
Better give me
that gun, son.

2105
01:18:58,133 --> 01:18:59,667
You can't eat with one hand.

2106
01:18:59,700 --> 01:19:02,233
Actually, you can, but I'll
give you the gun anyway.

2107
01:19:04,567 --> 01:19:06,833
Wait a minute,
this is an episode of insight.

2108
01:19:06,867 --> 01:19:08,133
Yep.

2109
01:19:08,167 --> 01:19:10,433
I saw it on your face
when you first came in here.

2110
01:19:10,467 --> 01:19:12,000
I can read your
chakras, too.

2111
01:19:12,033 --> 01:19:13,367
--Been around.

2112
01:19:13,400 --> 01:19:16,067
- Seen all sorts in my time.
- But they don't see me.

2113
01:19:16,100 --> 01:19:18,167
You learn things about people
in this business.

2114
01:19:18,200 --> 01:19:20,300
For instance,
they're bipeds.

2115
01:19:20,333 --> 01:19:22,900
Mmm, loaded too.

2116
01:19:22,933 --> 01:19:25,067
That's dangerous.

2117
01:19:25,100 --> 01:19:27,033
Look, can I have
my hamburger?

2118
01:19:27,067 --> 01:19:28,967
You know, some guys get sore

2119
01:19:29,000 --> 01:19:30,567
when you pull a gun on 'em.

2120
01:19:30,600 --> 01:19:33,000
And they don't
stop to think.

2121
01:19:33,033 --> 01:19:34,533
Why, you might've
even killed me.

2122
01:19:34,567 --> 01:19:36,600
Not meaning it, either.

2123
01:19:36,633 --> 01:19:39,200
- Such things happen.
- I know.

2124
01:19:39,233 --> 01:19:42,633
Better put this away before
somebody comes in and sees it.

2125
01:19:43,767 --> 01:19:45,200
Would you get me
my hamburger?

2126
01:19:45,233 --> 01:19:47,000
Okay, I'll keep it for you.

2127
01:19:47,033 --> 01:19:48,433
You can have it
anytime you want.

2128
01:19:48,467 --> 01:19:50,367
[All] At Alice's restaurant.

2129
01:19:57,233 --> 01:19:58,733
Funny thing, you dropping
in here this way.

2130
01:19:58,767 --> 01:20:01,633
- Why?
- I've dreamt of your
soft features.

2131
01:20:01,667 --> 01:20:04,100
--I'd like to have a boy
like you to help out here.

2132
01:20:04,133 --> 01:20:06,000
- Want a job?
- Sure, I want a job.

2133
01:20:06,033 --> 01:20:07,900
You ever worked
as a boy before?

2134
01:20:07,933 --> 01:20:09,700
--Your food and lodgings.

2135
01:20:09,733 --> 01:20:12,000
I got a shack here
in back of the restaurant.

2136
01:20:12,033 --> 01:20:13,867
- Tain't much--
- in fact, it sucks.

2137
01:20:13,900 --> 01:20:15,133
--Comfortable enough.

2138
01:20:15,167 --> 01:20:18,267
Radio, some flowers
in the garden, and the dog.

2139
01:20:18,300 --> 01:20:20,267
- And me.
- What do you say?

2140
01:20:20,300 --> 01:20:21,467
Give me my gun back.

2141
01:20:21,500 --> 01:20:22,867
--An awful chance,
aren't you?

2142
01:20:22,900 --> 01:20:24,500
I mean, offering me
a job this way.

2143
01:20:24,533 --> 01:20:26,167
Without knowing
anything about me?

2144
01:20:26,200 --> 01:20:28,000
You see, before i--

2145
01:20:28,033 --> 01:20:29,200
I gotta tell you, though,

2146
01:20:29,233 --> 01:20:30,867
there's one condition
attached to it.

2147
01:20:30,900 --> 01:20:33,467
You have to go to church
with me every Sunday morning.

2148
01:20:33,500 --> 01:20:34,967
Church?

2149
01:20:35,000 --> 01:20:37,100
- That's right.
- Forget it!

2150
01:20:37,133 --> 01:20:38,733
--Week, I work for myself.

2151
01:20:38,767 --> 01:20:42,267
On the seventh,
I work for the church.

2152
01:20:42,300 --> 01:20:43,567
I'm an Usher.

2153
01:20:43,600 --> 01:20:45,600
It wouldn't look right,
you living in my house

2154
01:20:45,633 --> 01:20:47,133
and not going to church.

2155
01:20:47,167 --> 01:20:49,967
Of course, that's only
an hour on Sunday mornings.

2156
01:20:50,000 --> 01:20:52,200
In the afternoons,
on fine days,

2157
01:20:52,233 --> 01:20:53,800
- we could go fishing.
- [All] Ahh.

2158
01:20:53,833 --> 01:20:55,933
Gee, that sounds swell.

2159
01:20:55,967 --> 01:20:57,600
Oh, and no mob ties.

2160
01:20:57,633 --> 01:20:59,233
You're learning fast.

2161
01:20:59,267 --> 01:21:02,767
I've entered
the twilight zone.

2162
01:21:02,800 --> 01:21:05,067
How do you like
my swingin' church, son?

2163
01:21:07,800 --> 01:21:11,600
* I've got a goofy hat
on my head *

2164
01:21:11,633 --> 01:21:13,367
* --i need you

2165
01:21:13,400 --> 01:21:16,600
Michelle pfeiffer
in the fabulous baker boys.

2166
01:21:16,633 --> 01:21:17,933
* where can you be?

2167
01:21:17,967 --> 01:21:19,733
He's in Kansas,
flipping burgers.

2168
01:21:19,767 --> 01:21:22,067
* I miss you so

2169
01:21:22,100 --> 01:21:23,500
it's an air filter piano.

2170
01:21:23,533 --> 01:21:26,000
* how I cried

2171
01:21:26,033 --> 01:21:27,767
- * and tried
- [servo beat-boxes]

2172
01:21:27,800 --> 01:21:29,867
* looking down
the lonely street *

2173
01:21:29,900 --> 01:21:33,067
oh, she's a regular
koko Taylor. Cha-cha.

2174
01:21:33,100 --> 01:21:34,433
Or irregular.

2175
01:21:34,467 --> 01:21:36,367
And now she's got a table
centerpiece on her head.

2176
01:21:36,400 --> 01:21:38,067
* --return here

2177
01:21:38,100 --> 01:21:40,167
* how I learned here--

2178
01:21:40,200 --> 01:21:41,433
now, let's see,
I've ordered the death

2179
01:21:41,467 --> 01:21:42,900
of ten, no,
twelve people today.

2180
01:21:42,933 --> 01:21:44,067
Pretty good day.

2181
01:21:44,100 --> 01:21:45,733
* why did you leave me--

2182
01:21:45,767 --> 01:21:48,733
* you told him to

2183
01:21:48,767 --> 01:21:51,767
* didn't you know

2184
01:21:51,800 --> 01:21:54,233
* I'd be forlorn--

2185
01:21:54,267 --> 01:21:55,900
* and green

2186
01:21:55,933 --> 01:21:58,167
* now I hope

2187
01:21:58,200 --> 01:22:00,333
* and pray

2188
01:22:00,367 --> 01:22:02,533
* that maybe someday

2189
01:22:02,567 --> 01:22:04,733
* I can say that I'm sorry

2190
01:22:04,767 --> 01:22:06,633
* please hear my plea--

2191
01:22:06,667 --> 01:22:08,400
* not guilty!

2192
01:22:08,433 --> 01:22:09,933
* where can you be?

2193
01:22:09,967 --> 01:22:12,033
The audience
is frankly stunned.

2194
01:22:12,067 --> 01:22:14,433
* where can you be?

2195
01:22:14,467 --> 01:22:17,967
[Servo harmonizes]
* where can you be?

2196
01:22:20,433 --> 01:22:22,033
"Where can you be."

2197
01:22:22,067 --> 01:22:23,567
Last call,
ladies and gentlemen.

2198
01:22:23,600 --> 01:22:27,200
Last call.

2199
01:22:27,233 --> 01:22:28,600
You were swell
in that, kitten.

2200
01:22:28,633 --> 01:22:30,900
- [Servo meows]
- Thanks.

2201
01:22:30,933 --> 01:22:33,133
Still thinking
about Jimmy, huh?

2202
01:22:33,167 --> 01:22:34,433
What makes you think that?

2203
01:22:34,467 --> 01:22:36,367
Oh, maybe the way
you sang that song.

2204
01:22:36,400 --> 01:22:38,033
Oh, now, look, kitten,
I know you've been--

2205
01:22:38,067 --> 01:22:39,400
- meow.
- --Searching for that kid
for two months.

2206
01:22:39,433 --> 01:22:40,667
Why don't you give it up?

2207
01:22:40,700 --> 01:22:42,567
He's probably
a thousand miles from here.

2208
01:22:42,600 --> 01:22:43,833
I'll tell you what we'll do.

2209
01:22:43,867 --> 01:22:45,067
When you get through tonight,
we'll go out

2210
01:22:45,100 --> 01:22:47,000
and paint the town.
You need some recreation.

2211
01:22:47,033 --> 01:22:48,733
I'll kill somebody for you.
Who do you want killed?

2212
01:22:48,767 --> 01:22:50,200
Okay, Charlie.

2213
01:22:52,900 --> 01:22:54,933
Ho, what a caboose. Hoo-hah.

2214
01:22:57,767 --> 01:22:59,867
Son, it's been two months,

2215
01:22:59,900 --> 01:23:02,500
and you haven't touched
your hamburger.

2216
01:23:02,533 --> 01:23:04,833
Sir, I just don't
understand the holy spirit.

2217
01:23:04,867 --> 01:23:06,167
Is it a bird?

2218
01:23:06,200 --> 01:23:08,333
What's the matter?
Not hungry?

2219
01:23:08,367 --> 01:23:10,233
How come i'm
the only customer?

2220
01:23:10,267 --> 01:23:12,300
Something's bothering you.

2221
01:23:12,333 --> 01:23:14,200
- What is it? Homesick?
- Uhh.

2222
01:23:14,233 --> 01:23:16,633
- No.
- I found a toenail
in my hamburger.

2223
01:23:16,667 --> 01:23:18,233
I thought you liked it here
pretty well.

2224
01:23:18,267 --> 01:23:19,400
Seem to be settling down.

2225
01:23:19,433 --> 01:23:21,233
I do like it, al.
It's not that.

2226
01:23:21,267 --> 01:23:23,300
In fact, it's the only time
I've ever really been happy.

2227
01:23:23,333 --> 01:23:25,300
But I want a salad.
Is that asking too much?

2228
01:23:25,333 --> 01:23:28,167
Spill it, son,
you can tell me.

2229
01:23:28,200 --> 01:23:29,567
Well, it's-- it's just
that I've been

2230
01:23:29,600 --> 01:23:30,967
thinking things over,
that's all.

2231
01:23:31,000 --> 01:23:32,300
- And I want new curtains.
- You wanna go back

2232
01:23:32,333 --> 01:23:34,233
and straighten yourself out?

2233
01:23:34,267 --> 01:23:36,867
Square accounts?
Take the load off your mind?

2234
01:23:36,900 --> 01:23:38,133
Yeah, I guess that's it.

2235
01:23:38,167 --> 01:23:39,967
Bring your trousers
in for dry-cleaning?

2236
01:23:40,000 --> 01:23:41,267
Find the courage to do it.

2237
01:23:41,300 --> 01:23:42,433
Change that old underwear?

2238
01:23:42,467 --> 01:23:43,700
Would you help me, al?

2239
01:23:43,733 --> 01:23:45,033
And don't mention god.

2240
01:23:45,067 --> 01:23:47,033
I've been waiting
to hear you say that, son.

2241
01:23:47,067 --> 01:23:49,067
So I prepared a song.

2242
01:23:49,100 --> 01:23:51,300
We'll go back
and face it together.

2243
01:23:51,333 --> 01:23:52,767
After they hear your story,

2244
01:23:52,800 --> 01:23:54,967
I'm positive they'll
give you a break.

2245
01:23:55,000 --> 01:23:56,400
Don't worry.

2246
01:23:56,433 --> 01:23:57,600
Ah, gee, that's swell.

2247
01:23:57,633 --> 01:23:59,067
Well, I feel better already.

2248
01:23:59,100 --> 01:24:01,833
Now tuck in to that beef.

2249
01:24:01,867 --> 01:24:04,167
You see, miss Reed, I couldn't
let Jimmy give himself up

2250
01:24:04,200 --> 01:24:06,367
unless he'd seen you first.

2251
01:24:06,400 --> 01:24:08,667
- Okay. Let's go.
- And I wanted to see
you too, Jimmy.

2252
01:24:08,700 --> 01:24:10,233
To explain
and tell you the truth--

2253
01:24:10,267 --> 01:24:11,833
- I never wore the shoes.
- Blake was in

2254
01:24:11,867 --> 01:24:13,400
the other room that night,
listening.

2255
01:24:13,433 --> 01:24:15,300
I had to say what I did,
or he'd've killed you.

2256
01:24:15,333 --> 01:24:18,233
- Huh.
- They tried to the night
they beat you up.

2257
01:24:18,267 --> 01:24:20,500
And, then, the things
you said weren't true.

2258
01:24:20,533 --> 01:24:22,033
Of course they weren't true.

2259
01:24:22,067 --> 01:24:24,567
Except for about
your lousy shoe career.

2260
01:24:24,600 --> 01:24:25,967
Oh, Jimmy, Blake's the cause

2261
01:24:26,000 --> 01:24:27,533
of all your trouble
and mine, too.

2262
01:24:27,567 --> 01:24:29,967
If he finds out you're here,
he'll kill US both.

2263
01:24:30,000 --> 01:24:32,000
No, he won't, because he's going
to the police station with me.

2264
01:24:32,033 --> 01:24:33,600
You and al can call the cops
and follow US.

2265
01:24:33,633 --> 01:24:34,933
Jimmy, wait! Jimmy!

2266
01:24:34,967 --> 01:24:36,033
Quack, quack, quack quack.

2267
01:24:36,067 --> 01:24:38,933
Again, proving
just how stupid he is.

2268
01:24:38,967 --> 01:24:42,233
So, how about a little sugar
for happy chef over here?

2269
01:24:42,267 --> 01:24:43,567
Organized crime,
please hold.

2270
01:24:43,600 --> 01:24:45,233
Organized crime,
please hold-- sir?

2271
01:24:48,133 --> 01:24:50,700
Let me guess.
It's your birthday.

2272
01:24:50,733 --> 01:24:52,733
- Hello, Jimmy.
- How's your hat? [Chuckles]

2273
01:24:52,767 --> 01:24:54,533
What brings you to see me?

2274
01:24:54,567 --> 01:24:56,200
Not in trouble again, are you?

2275
01:24:56,233 --> 01:24:57,600
No, but you are.

2276
01:24:57,633 --> 01:24:58,967
I'm giving myself up
to the police,

2277
01:24:59,000 --> 01:25:00,633
and you're coming with me.

2278
01:25:00,667 --> 01:25:01,967
You're taking a lot
for granted, aren't you?

2279
01:25:02,000 --> 01:25:03,500
Maybe I am.

2280
01:25:03,533 --> 01:25:06,200
But you're gonna tell everything
that's happened between US.

2281
01:25:06,233 --> 01:25:07,933
- And if I don't?
- You'll kill me?

2282
01:25:07,967 --> 01:25:09,967
The police are on their way
here to see that you do.

2283
01:25:10,000 --> 01:25:11,767
Now, let's see,
did I call them?... right.

2284
01:25:11,800 --> 01:25:14,667
Okay, Jimmy.

2285
01:25:14,700 --> 01:25:18,033
About time I went on the
straight and narr-- hi-keeba!

2286
01:25:18,067 --> 01:25:21,900
Well, that's
a weird position.

2287
01:25:21,933 --> 01:25:25,700
They're really
going to town in there.

2288
01:25:25,733 --> 01:25:28,033
Hey, does anyone
have an appointment?

2289
01:25:31,300 --> 01:25:32,433
[Gunshot]

2290
01:25:32,467 --> 01:25:35,033
His heart just exploded.

2291
01:25:35,067 --> 01:25:36,767
Well, so much for the whole

2292
01:25:36,800 --> 01:25:38,633
"he's coming with me"
scenario.

2293
01:25:41,333 --> 01:25:43,467
Uh, I accuse my parents.

2294
01:25:45,367 --> 01:25:47,267
I tried to take the gun
away from him.

2295
01:25:47,300 --> 01:25:50,167
- But it went off.
- Huh?

2296
01:25:50,200 --> 01:25:52,367
Oh, I know I've lied.
I've cheated.

2297
01:25:52,400 --> 01:25:55,333
- I've done a lot of things
that I shouldn't have done.
- And more.

2298
01:25:55,367 --> 01:25:57,900
But maybe I wouldn't have
started lying to my schoolmates

2299
01:25:57,933 --> 01:26:00,500
if I hadn't been ashamed
of my home life.

2300
01:26:00,533 --> 01:26:03,433
If I hadn't been ashamed
that my parents were--

2301
01:26:03,467 --> 01:26:06,633
- were denying--
- this is wild.

2302
01:26:06,667 --> 01:26:10,433
--The love and protection
that a boy needs.

2303
01:26:10,467 --> 01:26:11,900
The guidance
that sets him straight.

2304
01:26:11,933 --> 01:26:15,167
Maybe they should've
sworn him in.

2305
01:26:15,200 --> 01:26:17,067
And that's why...

2306
01:26:17,100 --> 01:26:18,733
I accuse my parents.

2307
01:26:18,767 --> 01:26:21,133
[All] Aah. Oh.

2308
01:26:21,167 --> 01:26:22,967
Is your hat flask empty yet?

2309
01:26:23,000 --> 01:26:24,867
That court reporter
is dreamy.

2310
01:26:27,033 --> 01:26:29,033
Seeing as it's your birthday,
we'll let you go.

2311
01:26:29,067 --> 01:26:30,967
- James Wilson--
- you dummy.

2312
01:26:31,000 --> 01:26:33,833
Your story is supported by much
of the evidence in this case.

2313
01:26:33,867 --> 01:26:36,533
And I think indicates clearly
that you are not guilty

2314
01:26:36,567 --> 01:26:38,033
of the killing
of Charles Blake.

2315
01:26:38,067 --> 01:26:39,367
Thanks! Well, bye.

2316
01:26:39,400 --> 01:26:40,800
--Count I find you
not guilty.

2317
01:26:40,833 --> 01:26:42,800
[Crowd murmurs]

2318
01:26:42,833 --> 01:26:44,767
Huh-- oh. Oh, "not" guilty!

2319
01:26:44,800 --> 01:26:47,167
- Oh.
- On the remaining counts

2320
01:26:47,200 --> 01:26:48,867
of having aided and abetted

2321
01:26:48,900 --> 01:26:50,500
in the transportation
and concealment

2322
01:26:50,533 --> 01:26:51,600
of stolen property,

2323
01:26:51,633 --> 01:26:53,300
- uh-oh.
- I find you guilty

2324
01:26:53,333 --> 01:26:55,533
and sentence you
to five years in state prison.

2325
01:26:55,567 --> 01:26:56,900
Hey, my dad went there.

2326
01:26:56,933 --> 01:26:58,500
That sentence
is hereby suspended.

2327
01:26:58,533 --> 01:27:00,733
And you are placed
on probation for two years.

2328
01:27:00,767 --> 01:27:02,533
- Thank god I'm white!
- You are to remain in

2329
01:27:02,567 --> 01:27:05,100
the custody of your parents
until you are 21.

2330
01:27:05,133 --> 01:27:06,333
During which time I hope

2331
01:27:06,367 --> 01:27:07,833
that you will
justify the confidence

2332
01:27:07,867 --> 01:27:09,167
- I am placing in you.
- Hah!

2333
01:27:09,200 --> 01:27:10,500
I will, your honor.

2334
01:27:10,533 --> 01:27:13,600
Oh, let's go to Jack Taylor's
and celebrate.

2335
01:27:13,633 --> 01:27:15,067
- Jimmy!
- Wait, wait,

2336
01:27:15,100 --> 01:27:17,433
he has to talk
to Doug llewelyn first.

2337
01:27:23,167 --> 01:27:24,700
He accused US.

2338
01:27:24,733 --> 01:27:27,567
Why don't you just
do it on the bench?

2339
01:27:27,600 --> 01:27:29,600
As for you,
Mr. and Mrs. Wilson.

2340
01:27:29,633 --> 01:27:31,367
You are not on trial here.

2341
01:27:31,400 --> 01:27:33,567
But you have seen
the tragedy brought about

2342
01:27:33,600 --> 01:27:35,333
by the neglect
your boy suffered.

2343
01:27:35,367 --> 01:27:36,800
You will roast in hell.

2344
01:27:36,833 --> 01:27:38,800
--The only parents
guilty of such neglect.

2345
01:27:38,833 --> 01:27:41,333
- I speak
to parents everywhere--
- message coming in!

2346
01:27:41,367 --> 01:27:43,033
- There it is.
- In the pursuit
of your own

2347
01:27:43,067 --> 01:27:44,767
--own pleasures
and occupations,

2348
01:27:44,800 --> 01:27:46,433
you neglect your children.

2349
01:27:46,467 --> 01:27:48,533
Realize now
before it is too late.

2350
01:27:48,567 --> 01:27:50,633
- Buy bonds.
- This might have been your boy.

2351
01:27:50,667 --> 01:27:51,767
Not that your boy would be

2352
01:27:51,800 --> 01:27:53,667
quite so thick-headed
as Jimmy.

2353
01:27:53,700 --> 01:27:55,367
I accuse my parents

2354
01:27:55,400 --> 01:27:58,600
brought to you
by Boone's farm.

2355
01:27:58,633 --> 01:28:01,333
The makers of this film
also accuse Hitler

2356
01:28:01,367 --> 01:28:03,167
and tojo and Mussolini!

2357
01:28:03,200 --> 01:28:05,367
We accuse them all.
Soon we'll accuse Stalin.

2358
01:28:05,400 --> 01:28:06,933
Seriously, Joel,
who would you accuse?

2359
01:28:06,967 --> 01:28:10,000
Oh, I don't really...

2360
01:28:21,733 --> 01:28:24,400
Okay, as we move
into the home stretch,

2361
01:28:24,433 --> 01:28:26,200
I thought it'd be nice
to read a letter.

2362
01:28:26,233 --> 01:28:28,300
So...

2363
01:28:28,333 --> 01:28:29,967
Uh, hi, Tom. Hi, crow.

2364
01:28:30,000 --> 01:28:31,367
Just getting ready
to read a letter.

2365
01:28:31,400 --> 01:28:33,067
Oh, no thank you, that's okay.

2366
01:28:33,100 --> 01:28:35,500
All we'd like is
just a cup of coffee.

2367
01:28:35,533 --> 01:28:37,800
[Cough] Hamburgers. [Cough]

2368
01:28:37,833 --> 01:28:39,533
Well, I'll just get going
on this letter, then.

2369
01:28:39,567 --> 01:28:40,700
Hamburgers. [Cough]

2370
01:28:40,733 --> 01:28:43,267
No, no thanks.
We're... not hungry?

2371
01:28:43,300 --> 01:28:45,633
Oh, I get it.
It's like in the movie.

2372
01:28:45,667 --> 01:28:48,267
How would you boys
like a hamburger?

2373
01:28:48,300 --> 01:28:49,500
Like that?

2374
01:28:49,533 --> 01:28:51,633
Finally, what
took you so long?

2375
01:28:51,667 --> 01:28:53,200
What a maroon.

2376
01:28:53,233 --> 01:28:54,833
Now.

2377
01:28:54,867 --> 01:28:56,600
Now what?

2378
01:28:56,633 --> 01:28:58,067
- [Bots sigh]
- No, no, no.

2379
01:28:58,100 --> 01:28:59,900
You stupid, stupid man.

2380
01:28:59,933 --> 01:29:01,267
Now, you present US

2381
01:29:01,300 --> 01:29:03,600
with a big, beefy char-broiled
hamburger "sammich"

2382
01:29:03,633 --> 01:29:06,167
and a French-fried potatoes
garnish like in the movie.

2383
01:29:06,200 --> 01:29:08,433
Uh, all I got
is this postcard.

2384
01:29:08,467 --> 01:29:10,300
D'oh. Crow, you talk to him.

2385
01:29:10,333 --> 01:29:12,833
You were supposed to get US

2386
01:29:12,867 --> 01:29:14,833
a char-broiled
hamburger sandwich

2387
01:29:14,867 --> 01:29:16,033
like in the movie.

2388
01:29:16,067 --> 01:29:19,567
[Sobs] What is happening
to this family?

2389
01:29:19,600 --> 01:29:21,067
Come on, honey.
Honey, honey.

2390
01:29:21,100 --> 01:29:22,867
There must be a pie cooling
in the ship someplace.

2391
01:29:22,900 --> 01:29:25,167
- A pie?
- It's just a movie, guys.

2392
01:29:25,200 --> 01:29:27,200
Jeez.

2393
01:29:29,833 --> 01:29:31,133
Anyway.

2394
01:29:31,167 --> 01:29:33,200
Thought we could
read this letter now.

2395
01:29:33,233 --> 01:29:34,900
Um, this says,

2396
01:29:34,933 --> 01:29:37,033
"for rent,
the barco rammer."

2397
01:29:37,067 --> 01:29:38,833
And it's from Peter Spears.

2398
01:29:38,867 --> 01:29:40,067
And on the back here--

2399
01:29:40,100 --> 01:29:41,900
let's put that on still store
in the back.

2400
01:29:41,933 --> 01:29:43,833
It says, "the barco rammer.

2401
01:29:43,867 --> 01:29:45,567
"Indisputably the finest.

2402
01:29:45,600 --> 01:29:48,333
"It will ram, it will pound,
it will press.

2403
01:29:48,367 --> 01:29:50,300
It will do what
you want it to do."

2404
01:29:50,333 --> 01:29:51,867
And then
he humorously writes,

2405
01:29:51,900 --> 01:29:53,867
"the perfect date
for crow and Tom."

2406
01:29:53,900 --> 01:29:56,933
Which I thought
was pretty... funny?

2407
01:29:56,967 --> 01:29:59,800
[Tank ratchets, clanks]

2408
01:30:02,633 --> 01:30:04,833
I accuse you, Joel.

2409
01:30:04,867 --> 01:30:07,033
Now, carefully.

2410
01:30:07,067 --> 01:30:09,967
Hand over
the hamburger sandwich.

2411
01:30:12,033 --> 01:30:13,400
Ahh.

2412
01:30:13,433 --> 01:30:14,600
Don't let him forget
the French-fried

2413
01:30:14,633 --> 01:30:16,300
- potatoes garnish.
- Right.

2414
01:30:16,333 --> 01:30:19,033
Joel, you magnificent bastard!
I read your menu!

2415
01:30:19,067 --> 01:30:21,167
Come on, we gotta beat
mighty messina, maggot!

2416
01:30:21,200 --> 01:30:22,800
Aah.

2417
01:30:26,467 --> 01:30:28,100
Uh, what do you think, sirs?

2418
01:30:28,133 --> 01:30:30,667
[Glass breaks]

2419
01:30:30,700 --> 01:30:33,400
[Stripper coughs]

2420
01:30:35,733 --> 01:30:37,633
Uh, sorry, Joel.
Didn't catch that.

2421
01:30:37,667 --> 01:30:39,867
We, uh, came this close
to losing...

2422
01:30:39,900 --> 01:30:41,700
- Rodney.
- Right, right.

2423
01:30:41,733 --> 01:30:43,367
Almost lost Rodney.

2424
01:30:43,400 --> 01:30:44,900
Is this enough, doctor f?

2425
01:30:44,933 --> 01:30:47,467
No way, frank. There's plenty
more frosting to shovel.

2426
01:30:47,500 --> 01:30:51,000
Oh, just go push the button,
you freaked-out maniac.

2427
01:30:51,033 --> 01:30:52,567
Uh, look, Rodney.

2428
01:30:52,600 --> 01:30:54,900
I'm sorry this whole thing
got out of hand.

2429
01:30:54,933 --> 01:30:57,467
I'd like to make it
worth your while.

2430
01:30:57,500 --> 01:30:59,300
Oh, no, that's--
that's all right.

2431
01:30:59,333 --> 01:31:01,133
That-- you've done enough.

2432
01:32:04,367 --> 01:32:07,100
[Dad laughs]

2433
01:32:08,233 --> 01:32:10,567
Well, what's so funny?

2434
01:32:13,733 --> 01:32:15,400
This has been
a presentation

2435
01:32:15,433 --> 01:32:17,000
from comedy central.

